**`_winner` needed no change** — it already filters `cell["status"] == "PASS"`, so ABORTED is excluded exactly as FAIL is.

### Red-checks (each reverted after)
Removing the abort wrapper → 5/7 new quickbench tests fail; removing `not_abortable` → both not_abortable tests fail; removing `abort=job.aborted` → wiring test fails; stopping synchronously instead of a daemon thread → 202-before-stop fails (5 s block); removing the one-stop guard → second-stop test fails; reading every ledger file → AC-2 test returns 3; removing the `RuntimeStopError` catch → the failure test raises; removing either `low_disk` payload → its tests fail.

### Found, not fixed / not verified
- **AC-1, one clause is not expressible:** "a missing-length body with a non-empty body" cannot reach 413 under HTTP/1.0 — a body with no `Content-Length` has no framing, and detecting one would need a blocking `rfile.peek()` that would hang every bodyless cancel (an existing test and the normal case). I implemented every observable form: header absent → bodyless cancel (202); header present with no usable number (`""`, `"six"`, `"-1"`) → 413; oversize → 413; non-JSON type → 415; invalid JSON → 400. Say the word if you want a different reading.
- **One small refactor beyond the letter of the plan:** `_stop_orphan` now uses a shared `_entry_stop_command()` so the `stop_command` parse has one definition (behaviour identical); `engines.refuse` gained `**payload` as the plan allowed.
- **Not verified:** the live "Stop now" (fakes only, per the order), and the app's ABORTED rendering (05-02's side).
- **Not mine in this tree:** `.gitignore` (`app/.build/`) and `app/**` are the parallel 05-02 worker's; I touched neither. I also did not write `05-01-SUMMARY.md` — it is outside `files_modified`.

